     "problem": "Russian translation uses 'поспешил' (perfective, masculine) but Danish 'skyndte mig' is past tense, common gender/neutral. 'Я поспешил' implies a male speaker and a completed action, while the Danish is a simple past statement. A more faithful and natural translation is 'Я спешил(а), чтобы успеть на автобус.'",
